  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 147 AM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nNext week will feature continued heat as the upper level dome of \nhigh pressure continues to linger over much of the Southern Plains. \nHeat indices will likely range from 100 to 105 degrees across most \nof the area each day through the week, with some areas that may \nbreach 105 to 110 degrees. Therefore, heat will remain the main \nmessage through the week with continued risk for heat related \nillnesses.\n\nTowards the tail end of the week, the ridge may retreat westward and \nopen the door for northwesterly flow aloft. This could bring a \nreturn to precipitation chances, but chances remain low at this time.",
